   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 3,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "HOW TO USE",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote",
    "ue_properties": {
     "widget_ue_connectable": {},
     "version": "7.8",
     "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
    }
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Ultimate H3 — how to use\n\n**Updates:** nodes and workflow live at [github.com/stuubszzz/Stubelius-Ultimate-H3](https://github.com/stuubszzz/Stubelius-Ultimate-H3). ComfyUI Manager → Update All (or `git pull` in custom_nodes/Stubelius-Ultimate-H3) keeps the nodes current. Live preview: put `taeh3.safetensors` in models/vae_approx and pick it on the Models node.\n\nWork top to bottom: **Setup → Models → Output → Director → Finish**. Everything is chosen up front; after a seed hunt only **WINNER** is left.\n\n## 1 · SETUP — how it's generated\n- **mode** — Speed / Hybrid / Quality / PDMD: *how* the video is made. The size is picked on the Output node: Speed goes up to 2K, the others up to 4K. Picking a mode fills the settings below with its preset:\n\n| | MP | steps | sampler | speedup LoRA | how it reaches your Output size |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Speed | 0.4 | 8 | res_multistep / simple | 1.0 | renders ≈480p, upscales up to 2K |\n| Hybrid | 0.5 | 10 | euler / beta | 0.75 | renders ≈540p, upscales up to 4K |\n| Quality | 0.98 | 20 | euler / beta | 0 (off) | native ≈768p; from 1080p a polish (1.5× by default) re-renders it bigger, up to 4K |\n| PDMD | 0.98 | 4 | euler / simple | PDMD LoRA 1.0 | native ≈768p in 4 steps, upscales up to 4K (no polish) |\n\n- **seeds** — how many full videos (with sound) to render, 1–4.\n- **steps / sampler / scheduler / megapixels / speedup strength** — the mode's preset; change any of them after picking the mode.\n- Changing anything here **re-renders**.\n\n## 2 · MODELS — what it runs on\n- **ref2va / fl2va** — Reference and First/Last-Frame checkpoints (safetensors or GGUF). Only the one the Director needs is loaded; Extend also uses fl2va.\n- **text encoder, video/audio VAE** — safetensors or GGUF text encoder.\n- **speedup LoRA** — turbo/lightx2v; its strength comes from Setup.\n- **pdmd lora** — PDMD mode only: `lora_model_0.safetensors` from huggingface.co/pdmd2026/pdmd_4NFE_lora, as published (converted on load).\n- **extra LoRA 1–2** — apply to every chunk. Chunk-specific LoRAs go in each Director chunk.\n- **speed & memory** — attention backend, Sage, Low VRAM attention + chunk feed-forward (less VRAM), Spectrum / H3 cache (faster, may soften).\n- **live preview** — tiny VAE for the **LIVE PREVIEW** panel next to the Director; off = ComfyUI's default preview on the Director.\n\n## 3 · OUTPUT — what comes out (set it now, change it any time)\n- **final resolution** — Speed: native (≈480p), 720p, 1080p, 2K. Hybrid: native (≈540p) up to 4K. Quality and PDMD: native (≈768p), 1080p, 2K, 4K. Switching mode keeps your size when the new mode has it. The short side lands exactly on the number, portrait too. 4K holds ≈100 MB of RAM per frame: keep 4K clips short, especially at 48/60 fps.\n- **final fps** — 24 = untouched; 48 / 60 via RIFE, length and sync kept.\n- **upscaler** — RTX VSR, or DLSS5 + Color Lock (more detail, original colours).\n- **quality polish** strength / steps / method — Quality mode at 1080p and up.\n- Output feeds only Finish, so changing it **never re-renders** the seeds.\n\n## 4 · DIRECTOR — what the video is\nPrompt/timeline, Reference or First/Last-Frame mode (with up to two **middle frames**: drag them along the timeline to set when the video reaches them), references, aspect, duration (longer than one chunk = Extend), seed, and a **LoRAs for this chunk** box per chunk. Text in PROMPT OVERRIDE replaces the timeline.\n\n## 5 · FINISH — pick the winner\n**winner** — which seed to finish; **0 = hold** after the seeds. That's the only choice left after a seed hunt.\n\n**Seed hunt:** set seeds = 3 and **winner = 0** (hold) and queue → watch Seed 1–3 → set winner 1–3 on Finish → queue again (seconds, from cache). Winner 1+ on the first run finishes that seed straight away. Don't touch Setup / Models / Director in between.\n\nTurbo modes can mumble dialogue (measured −31…−39 dB vs −14 dB) — for talking shots use Quality."
   ],
